Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||02-27-2000||07:12 PM||||I have been speaking to a few people in Utah and I think a new club is going to be made. So far there are 3 of us meeting this coming Saturday and I think it will grow quickly. The last club had quite a few members and I think I can get the list of old members. <B>FIEROCIOUS kidzwheelz</B> and <B>mwbackus</B> would you guys be interested or anyone else here in Utah?||||reg||14
Z||000001||kidzwheelz||02-27-2000||11:02 PM||||  Sounds like a good idea to me. I didn't realize the other club had disbanded. Must be why I couldn't find any info on it!||||reg||14
Z||000002||FIEROCIOUS||02-28-2000||04:29 PM||||Sounds great you have my full support, You said saturday? The 4th? I work and so does Kidzwheelz. Definatly count me in. Is Carl going to be in? Also a buddy of mine is interested too.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||02-28-2000||08:25 PM||||The old club, Wastach Fieros, kinda just fizzled out and the president moved to California. That's the guy Karl bought his green and white GT from. Somehow Stuart, the old president, got a few sets of Miller Woods turbo pipes and I now have a set of them. They are made for an auto Fiero though and I don't know if I can make them work, but I'm gonna try.<P>Not sure if Karl will be in it or not since he doesn't have a Fiero. If you know anyone that would be interested that's great. Of course I will be pushing for the autocroos to be part of the meetings  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. Lee, one the guys I am meeting with, used to autocross his 87GT and is wanting to start going again.<P>I think it would be great to have a club of people willing to help repair and maintain these little gems. Driving a long string of Fieros down the road is pretty cool too. Karl, Deanne and myself all drove to Peachdays last year and that was a blast. Maybe this year there will be many more driving to it than just three.<P>As soon as I meet with these guys I will know more and report back.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FIEROCIOUS||02-29-2000||05:00 AM||||Sounds great keep me posted! Also would you be interested in high speed autoX in wendover? In comparison SCCA sucks! You should make a showing, I was the first and only Fiero to compete. I was in the novice class but beat a few of the race prepared experts! With my all stock Fiero! This year it's gonna be butt whoopin time! He He He.....||||reg||1
Z||000005||SCCA FIERO||03-01-2000||06:59 PM||||Ya I plan to attend to Pro Solo in Wendover with the URSCCA. I haven't been yet, but I hear they hit 100+ on the straights and you get multiple laps. I couldn't make it last year because my motor was sitting on my driveway at the time  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||mwbackus||03-04-2000||10:15 PM||||Wow,<BR>I was out on a little vacation last week, and I missed out on all of this.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  <BR>Sounds good to have a club here in Utah though. I'm just happy that they have not made Fiero's illegal here yet, just about everything else is.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000007||Boxdin||03-05-2000||03:49 PM||||I hope one of you Utah guys scooped up that 88 Formula that was advertised in Auto Trader. It was in Keanne Utah,and  needed a trans etc, but was priced around 2,000, and had 92k orig miles. Best of all it was met red with tan, or butterscotch, or whatever you call the gold interior. ||||reg||6
Z||000008||SCCA FIERO||03-10-2000||08:13 PM||||Looks like it's a go. If you are interested, we will be meeting at Rice Stadium on April 2nd, the first autocross of 00. If you are interested in racing you need to be there around 9AM and plan on being there til about 4PM. If the other 3 Forum members show (kidz, Mike and FIEROIOUS) there should be 6 or 7 of us there... I'm telling a couple others that might show up as well. There is a guy(Lee Brown) from SLC that was a Karting champion 3 times here in Utah and is a strong runner in the Fiero (gonna get my butt whipped  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">). <P>If you are not interested in racing you can still come and talk and watch. <P>So who's interested?||||reg||14
Z||000009||SCCA FIERO||03-13-2000||11:38 PM||||There will be a meeting before the April 2nd autocross. It will be at Galaxy Diner in Bountiful from 7:00pm to 9:00pm on March 23. Anyone interested in going?||||reg||1
Z||000010||Shaun41178||03-14-2000||01:05 AM||||SCCA have an extra set of those turbo pipes?  I wouldn't mind taking ashot at them onmy car if you can't get them to work on your car.<P>How far is Nampa idaho from you?  I bid on an aluminum bow tie 60* V6 block and one the auction.  It probably won't cost too much to ship but if you are reasonably close I was hoping you might be able to go check it out for me.  I can give more details later if it might work.  Letr me know thanks.<P>shaun||||reg||1
Z||000011||SCCA FIERO||03-14-2000||02:25 PM||||Shaun, Nampa is about 400 miles from me. If it were 200 miles away I would check it out for you, but it's just too far away for me. <P>I don't have an extra set of those pipes, sure wish I did. I haven't decided if I can make them work or not, but if I can't get them to work, I will let you know.||||reg||1
